Z||000000||reddog||11-17-2001||11:24 PM||||I was considering purchasing the Fiero Store High performance cylinder heads for my GT. Has anyone put them on there vehicle? Are they worth the money? Are the vavles larger than stock or do they flow better?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||reddog||11-18-2001||12:55 AM||||Hello!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DR650SE||11-18-2001||03:22 AM||||I got them!  I havn't been able to drive the car since I put them on because of some more clutch problems I'm still working on.  They give the engine a sexy look.  Especially If you paint the trunk side with a can of engine spray paint.  They also give the engine a nice deeper sound.  When I asked people the same question, I got flamed by people who said It wasn't the best money spent and thatyour better off porting the stock manifolds.  Mine howevere were cracked in two on the firewall side due to the water that rolls off the trunk lid.  I figure if Im ganna replace parts I'm going to replace them with high quality/goodlooking parts.  At least on one of my cars.  One has a nice great looking engine and the other is more a autocross racer so i't more power with less show.  My answer is if your going for power, then port the manifolds if you can.  If you want a sexy look with a small power increase then get them if you don't mind dropping that dime.  What ever you choose is up to you.  Good luck and keep up updated. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||11-18-2001||03:55 AM||||Heads or headers?  Their headers are a good buy, and should add a few hp (so would ported manifolds, but the headers undineably look COOLER!)<P>Cylinder heads though?  IMHO, why not just do an engine swap then.  There are better motors out there than the 2.8.  Infact, it is HARD to pick a worse engine...<P>PS: I LOVE your seats man, you've made me want to try a set!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||reddog||11-18-2001||05:44 AM||||I was referring to the cylinder head set , it's supposed to have the si valves and hi-Performandce springs and the Fiero Store sells them for $549. dollars. I wasn't sure if it would be any better than purchasing the reconditioned ones so I thought I would check with the forum and see if anyones purchased them yet. I want to build the motor but there isn't any performance shops in this town that are worth a damn. As for putting a new motor in, I'd love to, I actually found a sight that sells a supercharged 3800 for around $3500. but I don't know of anyone that could install it and I checked with several people on the forum and it costs more to have someone install it than the motor costs itself. Add the extras: fuel pump, wiring, altenator, ecm, A/C, starter, Waterpump, ECT. and your looking at about $10,000+ for everything! That's alot of money to fork out at one time. If you have a contact that can do the work for less I'd love to know. As of this minute I've decided to do a little at a time. I've got a NX express system in the works from 1fst2m6. I figured if the heads from the Fiero Store may help performance a little, and I plan on doing a rebuild a little at a time. Besides with about 115,000 I figure a valve job would probably be in the near future anyway! What do you all, The forum members think? Anyway, any ideas or points of view would be helpful.I apologize if this seems like I'm rambling ,however it is 4:45 in the morning and I just closed down the bar had a few beers and figured I would check the forum . Well better go my Girlfriend is getting a little impatient and wanting to go home ! SEE YA!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou_dias||11-18-2001||09:36 AM||||I'm offering a set of ported and polished heads in the mall.  $500 - $100 after you send me your heads.  So $400 net + shipping.<BR>3 angle valve job and even the valves have been polished.  It uses new stock springs.  You don't need better than stock unles you plan to rev over 6200rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||avengador1||11-18-2001||05:17 PM||||Don't buy the heads. Buy all the parts to make the heads yourself. It will be cheaper, especially if your original heads are in half decent condition. Buy the reconditioned heads if your heads are no good. Put the new parts in and you will have to lap the new valves in so they seal correctly. The Fiero store high performance heads do not come ported or polished. You could do this yourself and save some money. That is what I did for mine.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||G-Nasty||11-19-2001||01:19 AM||||I spent a total $525 on my heads. The shop did a competition port and polish, installed SSI valves(fierostore) with felpro seals. They looked beautiful. They flowed perfect. My rocker arms were too tight...I adjusted valve lash according to Chiltons & Haynes. If I ever meet the authors I will kick their asses. After eliminating valve lash retighten nut 1/4 to 1 full turn and not 1 and a 1/2 turns like they say or you may ruin everything. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||lou_dias||11-19-2001||09:10 AM||||again mine would be a net of $400 + shipping done by a local reputable machine shop who hase worked on v6 Fiero heads before.  Rockers and guideplates not included.<BR>just send me back what I'll send you.  For the core credit.<P>I'll have pictures later this week, I just bought polaroid film and I have a scanner.||||reg||1
